abstract: >-
  BETS (Beam-Enhanced Time Shaping) is a research implementation for
  reliability-aware admission and serving of time-sensitive streams in
  industrial MU-MIMO networks. It jointly addresses frame scheduling,
  beamweight allocation, and uplink/downlink bandwidth partitioning under
  time-varying wireless channel conditions.

